{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED for deployment round 16 at exact clean head 9529e444c5be20b29d87afaf247370bccf54345b, against request git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c2d3f9148c40aee1413bdc0d08a2f689f7099761, promise git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8839cf27e1af75ae7d462dbd5a19f794aa7e4ec4, and artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:911fd560941339068b86f95e813cbd5ac9c90645.\n\n1. The admission-profile trust anchor and replay contract are still names, not a mechanically resolvable mechanism. The note says a parentless bundle commit is “put in force at base” by a ratified sequence statement, but nowhere defines the statement kind/body, who may activate it, how ratification and supersession select exactly one profile at an arbitrary base, the bootstrap/default profile for a genesis-v0 workroom, or the bundle tree and interpreter-contract grammar. The current workroom fold confirms the gap: its ratifiable kinds are assert, propose and three unrelated governance kinds; opaque kinds are recorded but not ratifiable, and no fold derives an admission profile. Repository-wide search finds no admission-profile, contract-version or profile-unavailable implementation outside this note. Therefore an auditor cannot independently derive the required profile OID, case 11's wrong-profile impostor has no executable oracle, and case 4's present/missing-interpreter controls have no defined resolver to exercise. Specify the canonical activation statement, authority, effective-at-base fold including bootstrap and rotation, bundle bytes/schema, contract-version lookup and unavailable result; add positive controls spanning two profile activations and a first batch, plus the missing-interpreter negative control.\n\n2. Ledger-entry authentication does not survive the key rotation the governing design calls the kernel's sole reserved event. The parent-role rule accepts a predecessor “signed by the seque